@id: scene.104_the_rising_tide
@when: Unknown.scene_104_the_rising_tide
@where: Realm/Physical/Unknown
@scope: narrative
@entities: [Darian, Kael, Renn, Sera, Teryn, Theran, Vairis]
@region: Unknown
@environment: coastal
@terrain_family: coastal
@spatial_scale_hint: massive

=segments:
  - line: 1
    type: narration
    text: "book 20"
  - line: 2
    type: narration
    text: "chapter 104-the rising tide"
  - line: 4
    type: narration
    text: "~~~The Second Song – Rising Tide~~~~"
  - line: 6
    type: narration
    text: "Prologue: The One They Called Vine"
  - line: 8
    type: narration
    text: "Among the grove giants who first came to the boundary, one stood apart."
  - line: 10
    type: narration
    text: "Not the largest – that was Stone‑Jaw, whose crystal‑veined face became a landmark."
  - line: 11
    type: narration
    text: "Not the fiercest – that would come later, when the war split their kind."
  - line: 12
    type: narration
    text: "This one was quieter, older in a way that had nothing to do with years."
  - line: 13
    type: narration
    text: "He moved like water over stone, and when the Nephoretti sang, he was always the first to turn his head."
  - line: 15
    type: narration
    text: "They began to watch him."
  - line: 16
    type: narration
    text: "Sera noticed it first: the way his eyes followed the birds, the clouds, the slow arc of the sun."
  - line: 17
    type: narration
    text: "He was tracking something."
  - line: 18
    type: narration
    text: "Not threats – the swamp giants did that."
  - line: 19
    type: narration
    text: "Not food – the grove giants ate stone and light."
  - line: 20
    type: narration
    text: "He was reading the sky."
  - line: 22
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“He’s waiting for something,”"
  - line: 24
    type: narration
    text: "The giant stood at the edge of the old road, his massive form silhouetted against the bruised sunset."
  - line: 25
    type: narration
    text: "His hide was the color of deep moss, shot through with pale crystal formations that spiraled like climbing vines – which was why, when they finally needed a name for him, they called him Vine."
  - line: 27
    type: narration
    text: "The first sign came from the mountains."
  - line: 29
    type: narration
    text: "The grove giants said nothing, but Sera saw the way their eyes tracked the sky."
  - line: 30
    type: narration
    text: "This was not just a hard winter."
  - line: 31
    type: narration
    text: "Something in the atmosphere was off."
  - line: 33
    type: narration
    text: "Kael felt it before anyone else – a change in the needle’s pulse that made the rhythm stumble, hesitate, as if the ancient structure was bracing against something."
  - line: 34
    type: narration
    text: "He stood at the edge of the plaza, one hand pressed against the fused stone of the wall, and watched the peaks to the south where the first snow was beginning to dust the volcanic rock."
  - line: 36
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "“It’s coming,”"
  - line: 38
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn followed his gaze."
  - line: 39
    type: narration
    text: "The mountains had been black and bare since they arrived, but now they wore a cap of white that seemed to glow in the pale afternoon light."
  - line: 40
    type: narration
    text: "The wind that swept down from them carried a sharpness that hadn’t been there yesterday."
  - line: 42
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“How bad?”"
  - line: 44
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Bad enough.”"
  - line: 45
    type: narration
    text: "Kael’s expression was troubled. “The pulse is weakening. Cold does something to the vrill currents – makes them sluggish. If we lose the pulse entirely, even for a day…”"
  - line: 47
    type: narration
    text: "He didn’t finish."
  - line: 48
    type: narration
    text: "He didn’t need to."
  - line: 49
    type: narration
    text: "The pulse was their shield against the giants, their anchor in this hostile land."
  - line: 50
    type: narration
    text: "Without it, the swamp giants would cross the ancient boundary."
  - line: 51
    type: narration
    text: "The grove giants would descend from the highlands."
  - line: 52
    type: narration
    text: "Everything they had built would be tested."
  - line: 54
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“We prepare,”"
  - line: 56
    type: narration
    text: "Renn was the obvious choice for the mission."
  - line: 57
    type: narration
    text: "He had led the rescue of Nessa’s group, knew how to move through the landscape without attracting giants, understood the terrain west of the needle better than anyone."
  - line: 58
    type: narration
    text: "When Teryn asked him, he agreed without hesitation."
  - line: 60
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "“I’ll take Sera,”"
  - line: 62
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“Bring them home,”"
  - line: 64
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 66
    type: narration
    text: "II."
  - line: 67
    type: narration
    text: "The Western Cave"
  - line: 69
    type: narration
    text: "They left at dawn, moving through the eastern marsh with the practiced silence of hunters."
  - line: 70
    type: narration
    text: "The wind was already picking up, carrying the scent of snow and something else – salt from the distant sea, and the sharp tang of ozone that spoke of storms gathering."
  - line: 72
    type: narration
    text: "Sera walked beside Renn, her voice a low hum that seemed to keep the pulse steady in his chest."
  - line: 73
    type: narration
    text: "She had grown into her gift without fully understanding it, her melodies becoming as natural to the settlement as the beat of the needle."
  - line: 74
    type: narration
    text: "When she sang, the crystal shards they carried glowed brighter."
  - line: 75
    type: narration
    text: "When she stopped, they dimmed."
  - line: 77
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“How far?”"
  - line: 79
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“Another day,”"
  - line: 81
    type: narration
    text: "They pressed on through the afternoon, the light fading early behind clouds that rolled in from the sea."
  - line: 82
    type: narration
    text: "By nightfall, they had reached the ridgeline that overlooked the coastal inlet."
  - line: 83
    type: narration
    text: "Below, the water was already rising, waves crashing against the cliffs with a fury that hadn’t been there yesterday."
  - line: 85
    type: narration
    text: "And there, carved into the bluff face, was the cave."
  - line: 87
    type: narration
    text: "They found the survivors huddled in a side chamber, their bioluminescence barely visible in the darkness."
  - line: 88
    type: narration
    text: "Their leader, a Nephoretti named Theran, had been watching the sea for days."
  - line: 90
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "“We knew someone would come,”"
  - line: 92
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“How many?”"
  - line: 94
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“About a dozen. Started with nearly thirty. Lost the others to the cliffs, to the giants, to…”"
  - line: 95
    type: narration
    text: "He gestured vaguely at the darkness. “We couldn’t find food. Couldn’t find shelter. This cave was the only place that felt safe.”"
  - line: 97
    type: narration
    text: "Renn looked at the survivors."
  - line: 98
    type: narration
    text: "They were thin, weak."
  - line: 99
    type: narration
    text: "They had been here since the landing, months ago, surviving on nothing but the faint vrill that seeped through the rock."
  - line: 100
    type: narration
    text: "It wasn’t enough."
  - line: 102
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "“We need to move,”"
  - line: 104
    type: narration
    text: "He didn’t finish."
  - line: 105
    type: narration
    text: "A sound interrupted him – a soft, insistent rush of water, coming from deeper in the cave."
  - line: 107
    type: narration
    text: "Sera’s hum faltered."
  - line: 108
    type: narration
    text: "“What’s that?”"
  - line: 110
    type: narration
    text: "Theran’s face went pale."
  - line: 111
    type: narration
    text: "“The tide."
  - line: 112
    type: narration
    text: "It’s coming in faster than usual."
  - line: 113
    type: narration
    text: "The lower passages flood when the sea rises."
  - line: 114
    type: narration
    text: "But it’s never done it this early.”"
  - line: 116
    type: narration
    text: "Renn felt a cold knot form in his stomach."
  - line: 117
    type: narration
    text: "The storm surge."
  - line: 118
    type: narration
    text: "It was already reaching the cave."
  - line: 120
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“We need to go. Now.”"
  - line: 122
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 124
    type: narration
    text: "III."
  - line: 125
    type: narration
    text: "Rising Water"
  - line: 127
    type: narration
    text: "They moved through the twisting passages as fast as the weak survivors could manage, following the faint pulse of the crystal shards that guided them toward the exit."
  - line: 128
    type: narration
    text: "But the water was faster."
  - line: 130
    type: narration
    text: "It rose around their ankles first, then their knees, then their waists."
  - line: 131
    type: narration
    text: "The passages that had been dry an hour ago were now narrow channels of icy seawater, and the roar of the storm outside had become a constant thunder that vibrated through the rock."
  - line: 133
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“The exit is blocked!”"
  - line: 134
    type: narration
    text: "one of the survivors shouted, her voice cracking with panic. “Water’s coming in from both ends!”"
  - line: 136
    type: narration
    text: "Renn forced himself to think."
  - line: 137
    type: narration
    text: "The crystal shards still glowed, but the pulse was distorted, echoing off the flooded passages."
  - line: 138
    type: narration
    text: "He closed his eyes, focused, and felt it: a different current, a deeper vibration that wasn’t coming from the needle at all."
  - line: 140
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "“There,”"
  - line: 142
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Sera
    text: "“We don’t know where it goes,”"
  - line: 144
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“We don’t have a choice.”"
  - line: 146
    type: narration
    text: "They climbed, the passage narrowing until they had to crawl, the roar of the storm fading behind them."
  - line: 147
    type: narration
    text: "The rock walls were slick with condensation, and in the darkness, Sera’s humming became the only light, her voice echoing strangely off the stone."
  - line: 149
    type: narration
    text: "Then the passage opened."
  - line: 151
    type: narration
    text: "They emerged into a chamber that took their breath away."
  - line: 153
    type: narration
    text: "It was vast, a natural cathedral carved by water over eons."
  - line: 154
    type: narration
    text: "Stalactites hung from the ceiling like frozen lightning, and at the center of the chamber was a pool of perfectly still water, its surface reflecting light that seemed to come from nowhere."
  - line: 155
    type: narration
    text: "Crystal formations lined the walls, and in their depths, something moved – slow pulses of light, rhythmic and deliberate, like a heartbeat."
  - line: 157
    type: narration
    text: "Sera’s humming stopped."
  - line: 158
    type: narration
    text: "The crystals responded, their pulses quickening, and for a moment the entire chamber vibrated with a sound that was not quite music, not quite language."
  - line: 160
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Theran
    text: "“What is this place?”"
  - line: 162
    type: narration
    text: "Renn had no answer."
  - line: 163
    type: narration
    text: "He felt the pulse in his own chest, resonating with something vast and patient, something that had been here long before the Nephoretti, before the Aeon Keepers, before anything that could be called memory."
  - line: 165
    type: narration
    text: "But there was no time to explore."
  - line: 166
    type: narration
    text: "Behind them, water was beginning to seep into the chamber, trickling down the passage they had climbed."
  - line: 168
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "“We need to keep moving,”"
  - line: 170
    type: narration
    text: "Sera began to hum again, and this time the crystals answered."
  - line: 171
    type: narration
    text: "Their light intensified, forming patterns that seemed to point toward a narrow fissure in the far wall."
  - line: 172
    type: narration
    text: "The survivors moved toward it, climbing over fallen stone and ancient flowstone formations."
  - line: 174
    type: narration
    text: "The water rose faster now, pouring into the chamber with a sound like a waterfall."
  - line: 175
    type: narration
    text: "Renn helped the last of the survivors through the fissure, then turned to see Sera standing at the edge of the pool, her hand outstretched toward the still water."
  - line: 177
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Sera!”"
  - line: 179
    type: narration
    text: "She didn’t seem to hear him."
  - line: 180
    type: narration
    text: "Her humming had become a melody he had never heard before, something ancient and sorrowful, and the pool was responding."
  - line: 181
    type: narration
    text: "Ripples spread across its surface, and beneath them, something stirred – a shape, vast and indistinct, rising from the depths."
  - line: 183
    type: narration
    text: "Then the water reached her knees, and she gasped, the spell broken."
  - line: 184
    type: narration
    text: "Renn grabbed her arm and pulled her toward the fissure as the chamber behind them filled with a sound that was almost a voice – a single, resonant tone that seemed to shake the mountain itself."
  - line: 186
    type: narration
    text: "They scrambled through the fissure, scraping stone, and found themselves in a narrow chimney that led upward."
  - line: 187
    type: narration
    text: "Above, faint light showed – the surface, perhaps, or the last of the dying day."
  - line: 189
    type: narration
    text: "They climbed."
  - line: 191
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 193
    type: narration
    text: "IV."
  - line: 194
    type: narration
    text: "The Storm"
  - line: 196
    type: narration
    text: "They emerged on a ridge overlooking the settlement just as the first snow began to fall."
  - line: 198
    type: narration
    text: "Below, the needle pulsed weakly, its light barely visible through the white."
  - line: 199
    type: narration
    text: "The wall was crowded with figures, and even from this distance, Renn could see the fear in their movements."
  - line: 201
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "“We need to get down,”"
  - line: 203
    type: narration
    text: "Sera began to sing."
  - line: 205
    type: narration
    text: "It wasn’t the humming she used in the settlement, or the melody she had found in the chamber."
  - line: 206
    type: narration
    text: "It was something new – a call, pure and simple, that rose above the wind and cut through the storm."
  - line: 208
    type: narration
    text: "Below, the needle answered."
  - line: 210
    type: narration
    text: "Its light flared, steadied, and for a moment the pulse was strong enough to feel even here."
  - line: 211
    type: narration
    text: "The figures on the wall turned toward the ridge, and Teryn’s voice echoed across the valley."
  - line: 213
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“They’re coming! Open the gate!”"
  - line: 215
    type: narration
    text: "They descended as the storm closed in, the snow thickening until the world was nothing but white and the faint glow of the needle ahead."
  - line: 216
    type: narration
    text: "Renn carried one of the survivors on his back; others leaned on each other, stumbling, falling, rising again."
  - line: 218
    type: narration
    text: "By the time they reached the gate, the storm was full upon them."
  - line: 219
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn was there, pulling them through, counting heads, her face tight with worry."
  - line: 221
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“All of them,”"
  - line: 223
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“And you.”"
  - line: 224
    type: narration
    text: "She looked past him, at Sera, whose face was pale and streaked with tears. “What happened out there?”"
  - line: 226
    type: narration
    text: "Sera shook her head."
  - line: 227
    type: narration
    text: "“I don’t know."
  - line: 228
    type: narration
    text: "There was a chamber."
  - line: 229
    type: narration
    text: "A pool."
  - line: 230
    type: narration
    text: "Something… something was there.”"
  - line: 232
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“Later,”"
  - line: 234
    type: narration
    text: "They sheltered in the needle’s base, where the walls were thickest and the pulse could be felt through the stone."
  - line: 235
    type: narration
    text: "Several hundred survivors now, huddled together against the cold, their voices rising in a work‑song that had become something more – a hymn, perhaps, or a prayer."
  - line: 237
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn stood at the edge of the chamber, watching the pulse flicker in the crystal veins."
  - line: 238
    type: narration
    text: "Kael was beside her, his hand pressed against the wall."
  - line: 240
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "“It’s holding,”"
  - line: 242
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“It will last as long as it lasts.”"
  - line: 243
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn’s voice was steady, but her eyes were fixed on the darkness beyond the walls. “We’ll survive. We’ve survived worse.”"
  - line: 245
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“Have we?”"
  - line: 247
    type: narration
    text: "She had no answer for that."
  - line: 248
    type: narration
    text: "A few months, and already they had lost so many."
  - line: 249
    type: narration
    text: "The thought of what winter might bring was a weight she carried in her chest, heavier than any stone."
  - line: 251
    type: narration
    text: "Behind them, Sera sat with Renn, her voice a thread of melody that wove through the pulse."
  - line: 252
    type: narration
    text: "She was singing the song she had found in the chamber, and the crystal veins were responding, their light brightening, their rhythm steadying."
  - line: 254
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“What did you find?”"
  - line: 256
    type: narration
    text: "Sera’s eyes were distant."
  - line: 257
    type: narration
    text: "“Something old."
  - line: 258
    type: narration
    text: "Something that was there before The Keepers, before the needles, before anything."
  - line: 259
    type: narration
    text: "It’s sleeping, I think."
  - line: 260
    type: narration
    text: "Or waiting.”"
  - line: 262
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Waiting for what?”"
  - line: 264
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“For us. For the right song.”"
  - line: 265
    type: narration
    text: "Sera looked at her hands, then at the pulse flickering in the walls. “The pool is rising. When the water recedes, we can go back. We need to go back.”"
  - line: 267
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn nodded slowly."
  - line: 268
    type: narration
    text: "She didn’t understand what Sera had found, but she understood what it meant: the southern continent held secrets that could change everything."
  - line: 269
    type: narration
    text: "And those secrets were waiting, patient as stone, for the moment when the song was strong enough to wake them."
  - line: 271
    type: narration
    text: "Outside, the storm howled."
  - line: 272
    type: narration
    text: "Inside, the survivors sang."
  - line: 274
    type: narration
    text: "And the needle’s pulse beat on, steady for now, waiting for the tide to turn."
  - line: 276
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 278
    type: narration
    text: "V."
  - line: 279
    type: narration
    text: "Winter’s Heart"
  - line: 281
    type: narration
    text: "The cold settled into the needle like a living thing."
  - line: 283
    type: narration
    text: "It seeped through the fused stone walls, crawled up from the frozen ground, pressed against the crystal veins until their light dimmed to the faintest glimmer."
  - line: 284
    type: narration
    text: "The pulse that had guided them since landing became a thread stretched thin – there, then gone, then there again, each beat a question rather than a certainty."
  - line: 286
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn stood at the base of the spire, her hand pressed against the largest crystal vein."
  - line: 287
    type: narration
    text: "The stone was cold enough to burn, but she didn’t pull away."
  - line: 288
    type: narration
    text: "She needed to feel it."
  - line: 289
    type: narration
    text: "Needed to know when it stopped."
  - line: 291
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“It’s holding,”"
  - line: 293
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Barely.”"
  - line: 294
    type: narration
    text: "She turned to face the chamber where the survivors had gathered. A couple hundred of them now, pressed together for warmth, their bioluminescence the only light besides the dying crystal. Children – not children, not really, but the thought‑seeds had manifested with something like youth, and some of them looked so young – huddled in the center, wrapped in woven reeds and whatever scraps of cloth they had salvaged from the landing."
  - line: 296
    type: narration
    text: "The storm outside had not stopped for weeks."
  - line: 297
    type: narration
    text: "Snow piled against the walls, burying the lower levels, sealing the fissure that led to the chamber beneath."
  - line: 298
    type: narration
    text: "The scouts who had tried to go beyond the wall had turned back within minutes, their bodies unable to withstand the wind."
  - line: 300
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Vairis
    text: "“We need more heat,”"
  - line: 302
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“We burn them,”"
  - line: 304
    type: narration
    text: "Vairis’s jaw tightened, but she nodded."
  - line: 306
    type: narration
    text: "Sera began to sing."
  - line: 307
    type: narration
    text: "It was not the humming she used during work, or the melodies she had found in the flooded chamber."
  - line: 308
    type: narration
    text: "This was something older, something that seemed to rise from the stone itself."
  - line: 309
    type: narration
    text: "Her voice filled the needle’s base, and one by one, the others joined her – not because they knew the words, but because the pulse was fading and the song was the only thing that pushed back the silence."
  - line: 311
    type: narration
    text: "The crystal veins flickered, steadied, flickered again."
  - line: 312
    type: narration
    text: "For a few heartbeats, the pulse beat strong."
  - line: 313
    type: narration
    text: "Then it faltered."
  - line: 315
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn closed her eyes."
  - line: 316
    type: narration
    text: "She had no voice for singing – her gift was not sound but stone, the geomancy that had built the walls around them."
  - line: 317
    type: narration
    text: "But she pressed her hands against the crystal and pushed her will into it, feeding it what little vrill she could spare."
  - line: 319
    type: narration
    text: "Around her, others did the same."
  - line: 320
    type: narration
    text: "Those who could shape stone added their strength to the walls, sealing cracks where the cold slipped through."
  - line: 321
    type: narration
    text: "Those who could sense water redirected the melt that seeped through the foundation."
  - line: 322
    type: narration
    text: "Those who had only their voices gave those too."
  - line: 324
    type: narration
    text: "The pulse held."
  - line: 326
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 328
    type: narration
    text: "VI."
  - line: 329
    type: narration
    text: "The Chamber"
  - line: 331
    type: narration
    text: "Deep into winter, the snow finally stopped."
  - line: 333
    type: narration
    text: "It was not a thaw – the cold remained, a weight that made every breath a labor – but the wind died, and for the first time in weeks, they could see beyond the wall."
  - line: 334
    type: narration
    text: "The swamp was a white plain, featureless and silent."
  - line: 335
    type: narration
    text: "The ancient stones that marked the boundary were buried."
  - line: 336
    type: narration
    text: "And far to the south, where the highlands rose, the peaks gleamed like the edge of a blade."
  - line: 338
    type: narration
    text: "Renn found Teryn on the wall, wrapped in layers of woven reed, her breath misting in the still air."
  - line: 340
    type: dialogue
    speaker: he
    text: "“The fissure is clear,”"
  - line: 342
    type: narration
    text: "She had been expecting this."
  - line: 343
    type: narration
    text: "The chamber beneath the needle had called to her since Renn first described it – the pool, the crystals, the presence that Sera had stirred with her song."
  - line: 344
    type: narration
    text: "But winter had sealed it away."
  - line: 345
    type: narration
    text: "Now, with the storm broken, they had a chance to understand what lay beneath them."
  - line: 347
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“Sera goes,”"
  - line: 349
    type: narration
    text: "Renn nodded."
  - line: 350
    type: narration
    text: "“Kael should come."
  - line: 351
    type: narration
    text: "He can read the pulse better than any of us.”"
  - line: 353
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Agreed.”"
  - line: 355
    type: narration
    text: "They descended through the fissure an hour later, their bioluminescence casting pale light on walls that had not seen warmth in months."
  - line: 356
    type: narration
    text: "The passage was narrow, forcing them to crawl in places, and the cold clung to the stone like a second skin."
  - line: 357
    type: narration
    text: "But as they dropped lower, the air changed – warmer, heavier, tinged with something that made Teryn’s skin prickle."
  - line: 359
    type: narration
    text: "They emerged into the chamber."
  - line: 361
    type: narration
    text: "The pool was lower than Renn had described, the water’s surface reflecting light that came from nowhere."
  - line: 362
    type: narration
    text: "The crystal formations along the walls pulsed with a rhythm that matched the needle’s – fainter here, but steadier, as if the cold had not reached this deep."
  - line: 364
    type: narration
    text: "And at the pool’s bottom, visible through the clear water, was a door."
  - line: 366
    type: narration
    text: "It was not stone, not crystal, but something that seemed to exist between states, its surface rippling with light that had no source."
  - line: 367
    type: narration
    text: "Patterns moved across it – spirals, waves, geometries that hurt to look at."
  - line: 368
    type: narration
    text: "And beneath the door, a presence."
  - line: 370
    type: narration
    text: "Sera knelt at the pool’s edge, her hand hovering above the water."
  - line: 371
    type: narration
    text: "“It’s waiting,” she whispered."
  - line: 372
    type: narration
    text: "“Not sleeping."
  - line: 373
    type: narration
    text: "Waiting.”"
  - line: 375
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“For what?”"
  - line: 377
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“For the right voice. The right song.”"
  - line: 378
    type: narration
    text: "Sera’s eyes were distant, focused on something none of them could see. “It’s been waiting a long time.”"
  - line: 380
    type: narration
    text: "Kael pressed his hand against the nearest crystal formation."
  - line: 381
    type: narration
    text: "“The pulse is stronger here."
  - line: 382
    type: narration
    text: "This chamber is the heart of the needle."
  - line: 383
    type: narration
    text: "Whatever is behind that door –” He stopped, his face going pale."
  - line: 385
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“What?”"
  - line: 386
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn demanded."
  - line: 388
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“It’s aware. Not awake, but aware. It knows we’re here.”"
  - line: 390
    type: narration
    text: "The water in the pool stirred, a single ripple spreading from the center to the edges."
  - line: 391
    type: narration
    text: "The crystal formations brightened, then dimmed, and for a moment, Teryn felt something brush against her consciousness – vast, patient, impossibly old."
  - line: 393
    type: narration
    text: "Then the moment passed."
  - line: 394
    type: narration
    text: "The water stilled."
  - line: 395
    type: narration
    text: "The presence withdrew."
  - line: 397
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“We should go,”"
  - line: 399
    type: narration
    text: "He was right."
  - line: 400
    type: narration
    text: "A trickle was seeping into the chamber from a crack in the far wall – melt from above, finding its way down."
  - line: 401
    type: narration
    text: "Before long, the pool would be full again."
  - line: 402
    type: narration
    text: "By the next day, the passage would be impassable."
  - line: 404
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn looked at the door, at the light that still rippled beneath the water."
  - line: 405
    type: narration
    text: "Something was down there."
  - line: 406
    type: narration
    text: "Something that had been waiting since before The Keepers, before Tiamat, before anything that could be called memory."
  - line: 408
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“We come back,”"
  - line: 410
    type: narration
    text: "Sera nodded slowly."
  - line: 411
    type: narration
    text: "“The song will be stronger then."
  - line: 412
    type: narration
    text: "It will answer.”"
  - line: 414
    type: narration
    text: "They climbed back to the surface, and behind them, the water rose, sealing the chamber once more."
  - line: 416
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 418
    type: narration
    text: "VII."
  - line: 419
    type: narration
    text: "The Thaw"
  - line: 421
    type: narration
    text: "Spring came not as a season but as a breaking."
  - line: 423
    type: narration
    text: "The ice that had locked the swamp cracked with sounds like thunder, sending sheets of white sliding into the channels."
  - line: 424
    type: narration
    text: "The snow on the walls began to run, turning the plaza into a marsh until the survivors dug channels to drain it."
  - line: 425
    type: narration
    text: "And from the south, warm winds swept up from the sea, carrying the smell of wet earth and growing things."
  - line: 427
    type: narration
    text: "Four hundred years, the Igigi had calculated, and they were right."
  - line: 428
    type: narration
    text: "The light was back."
  - line: 429
    type: narration
    text: "But Kael’s face was not joyful."
  - line: 430
    type: narration
    text: "They will come again, he said."
  - line: 431
    type: narration
    text: "Not soon."
  - line: 432
    type: narration
    text: "But they will come."
  - line: 434
    type: narration
    text: "The Long Calm lasted nearly three thousand years."
  - line: 435
    type: narration
    text: "Generations were born, lived, and died in the sun."
  - line: 436
    type: narration
    text: "The First Shadow became a story, then a myth, then a warning that only the Igigi and the oldest giants still believed."
  - line: 438
    type: narration
    text: "On the first day the giants returned to the boundary."
  - line: 440
    type: narration
    text: "They came in ones and twos at first – the big ones from the swamp, their jade‑green and charcoal hides streaked with mud, their eyes fixed on the settlement."
  - line: 441
    type: narration
    text: "They did not attack."
  - line: 442
    type: narration
    text: "They simply watched, as if waiting to see what had survived the cold."
  - line: 444
    type: narration
    text: "Within a few days, they were a ring around the plaza, a loose semicircle that extended from the eastern marsh to the western ridge."
  - line: 445
    type: narration
    text: "The survivors stood on the wall, watching."
  - line: 447
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Vairis
    text: "“More than we’ve ever seen at once,”"
  - line: 449
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“They’re testing,”"
  - line: 451
    type: narration
    text: "It had held."
  - line: 452
    type: narration
    text: "Barely."
  - line: 453
    type: narration
    text: "The crystal veins in the needle’s base were dark in places, the pulse a thin thread compared to what it had been before winter."
  - line: 454
    type: narration
    text: "But it was there."
  - line: 455
    type: narration
    text: "The giants could feel it, could feel the boundary it created, and they did not cross."
  - line: 457
    type: narration
    text: "But they did not leave, either."
  - line: 459
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“They’re waiting for something,”"
  - line: 461
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn felt the weight of his words."
  - line: 462
    type: narration
    text: "The giants were not mindless."
  - line: 463
    type: narration
    text: "The grove giants, especially, had shown intelligence, strategy."
  - line: 464
    type: narration
    text: "If they were communicating with the swamp giants, if they were forming some kind of alliance…"
  - line: 466
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“We need to find survivors,”"
  - line: 468
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“We’ll need scouts,”"
  - line: 470
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Then we start with scouts,”"
  - line: 471
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn agreed. “And we send word to any survivors who can hear us.”"
  - line: 473
    type: narration
    text: "She turned to Sera, who stood at the edge of the wall, her voice a low hum that seemed to harmonize with the pulse."
  - line: 475
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Can you do it? Call to them? Let them know we’re here?”"
  - line: 477
    type: narration
    text: "Sera’s eyes were distant, focused on something beyond the horizon."
  - line: 478
    type: narration
    text: "“The pulse can carry sound."
  - line: 479
    type: narration
    text: "If I sing at the right frequency, the crystal veins will transmit it."
  - line: 480
    type: narration
    text: "Anyone who can feel the pulse will hear.”"
  - line: 482
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Then sing.”"
  - line: 484
    type: narration
    text: "Sera closed her eyes."
  - line: 485
    type: narration
    text: "Her voice rose, not loud but clear, a single note that seemed to hang in the air."
  - line: 486
    type: narration
    text: "The crystal veins in the needle flickered, pulsed, and the note multiplied, echoing out across the swamp, across the highlands, across the cliffs where the sea crashed against stone."
  - line: 488
    type: narration
    text: "For a moment, everything was silent."
  - line: 489
    type: narration
    text: "The giants at the boundary went still, their massive heads lifting as if listening."
  - line: 490
    type: narration
    text: "The wind itself seemed to pause."
  - line: 492
    type: narration
    text: "Then the answer came."
  - line: 494
    type: narration
    text: "It was faint, distorted by distance and terrain, but unmistakable."
  - line: 495
    type: narration
    text: "A pulse, not the needle’s, but something like it – a voice, or many voices, raised in response."
  - line: 497
    type: narration
    text: "Sera opened her eyes."
  - line: 498
    type: narration
    text: "Tears streaked her face, but she was smiling."
  - line: 500
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“They heard. They’re coming.”"
  - line: 502
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 504
    type: narration
    text: "VIII."
  - line: 505
    type: narration
    text: "The Gathering"
  - line: 507
    type: narration
    text: "They came in waves."
  - line: 509
    type: narration
    text: "The first to arrive were the ones who had been closest – a group from the eastern hills, led by a Nephoretti named Darian who had survived the winter in a cave system, living on nothing but frozen roots and the faint vrill that seeped from the stone."
  - line: 510
    type: narration
    text: "They had heard the pulse through the long nights, had followed it through the thaw, and when Sera’s song had called, they had been close enough to answer within days."
  - line: 512
    type: narration
    text: "Then came the southern groups, from the coastal cliffs and the tidal flats."
  - line: 513
    type: narration
    text: "Their numbers were smaller – a handful here, a pair there, sometimes just two survivors who had kept each other alive through the cold."
  - line: 514
    type: narration
    text: "They brought stories of giants that hunted in the deep snow, of caves that had flooded, of friends who had not made it."
  - line: 516
    type: narration
    text: "By the end of spring, the settlement had grown to several hundred."
  - line: 518
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn stood on the wall each evening, watching the new arrivals trickle in, learning names."
  - line: 519
    type: narration
    text: "Some of them brought skills she hadn’t known they needed – a woman named Cora who could sense mineral deposits beneath the earth, a man named Veth whose geomancy was strong enough to shape the volcanic glass from the highlands into tools sharper than any stone."
  - line: 521
    type: narration
    text: "And some brought news."
  - line: 523
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“The grove giants are moving,”"
  - line: 524
    type: narration
    text: "Darian reported, his face grim. “They’ve been building something in the highlands. Structures, like walls, but not for defense. I saw them from the ridge before the snow closed in.”"
  - line: 526
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“What kind of structures?”"
  - line: 528
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“I don’t know. But they’re organized. They have leaders. The smaller ones take orders from the bigger ones, and they all work together. If they decide to come at us again…”"
  - line: 530
    type: narration
    text: "He didn’t finish."
  - line: 531
    type: narration
    text: "He didn’t need to."
  - line: 533
    type: narration
    text: "That night, Teryn called a council."
  - line: 534
    type: narration
    text: "Kael, Renn, Vairis, Sera, Nessa from the highlands group, Ione from the cliffs, Darian from the hills – everyone who had led survivors through the winter."
  - line: 536
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“We need to make a decision,”"
  - line: 538
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“The grove giants are the most intelligent,”"
  - line: 540
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Or maybe they’re the ones we should fear most,”"
  - line: 541
    type: narration
    text: "Nessa countered. “I saw what they did in the highlands. They herded us like animals. They could have killed us any time, but they chose not to. That’s not mercy – that’s strategy. They were waiting to see what we would do.”"
  - line: 543
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Sera
    text: "“Then we show them,”"
  - line: 545
    type: narration
    text: "The council fell silent."
  - line: 546
    type: narration
    text: "It was not the first time Sera had spoken in these meetings, but her words carried a weight now – a connection to something they did not fully understand."
  - line: 547
    type: narration
    text: "When she sang, the needle answered."
  - line: 548
    type: narration
    text: "When she spoke of the chamber, of the presence beneath the pool, they listened."
  - line: 550
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“How?”"
  - line: 552
    type: narration
    text: "Sera looked toward the south, toward the highlands where the grove giants were building their structures."
  - line: 553
    type: narration
    text: "“The same way we reached the survivors."
  - line: 554
    type: narration
    text: "The pulse can carry more than sound."
  - line: 555
    type: narration
    text: "It can carry intention."
  - line: 556
    type: narration
    text: "If I sing at the right frequency, if we all sing, the giants will feel it."
  - line: 557
    type: narration
    text: "They’ll know we want to build, not destroy.”"
  - line: 559
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Darian
    text: "“And if they don’t?”"
  - line: 561
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Then we try again. And again. Until they understand.”"
  - line: 562
    type: narration
    text: "Sera’s voice was steady, her eyes clear. “That’s what we’re here for. That’s what The Keepers sent us to do. Not to fight. To teach. To build. To sing.”"
  - line: 564
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn looked at the faces around her."
  - line: 565
    type: narration
    text: "They were tired, worn thin by winter and loss and the constant weight of survival."
  - line: 566
    type: narration
    text: "But there was something else there, too – something that had grown in the dark months, when the pulse was fading and the song was the only thing that held them together."
  - line: 568
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“We try,”"
  - line: 570
    type: narration
    text: "She stood, looking out at the settlement below – the walls, the shelters, the needle rising against the sunset."
  - line: 571
    type: narration
    text: "Several hundred survivors."
  - line: 572
    type: narration
    text: "Not enough to conquer, but enough to endure."
  - line: 574
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“Spring is here,”"
  - line: 576
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 578
    type: narration
    text: "IX."
  - line: 579
    type: narration
    text: "The First Note"
  - line: 581
    type: narration
    text: "Spring had announced itself with thunder and running water, but the cold refused to surrender."
  - line: 583
    type: narration
    text: "After the thaw, snow still clung to the northern slopes of the plaza wall, and the morning wind carried teeth that reminded Teryn of the deep winter."
  - line: 584
    type: narration
    text: "The marsh had become a maze of open channels and treacherous ice, and the giants that ringed the settlement had not withdrawn."
  - line: 585
    type: narration
    text: "They waited, patient as stone, their eyes following every movement on the wall."
  - line: 587
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“They’re not attacking,”"
  - line: 589
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“They’re watching,”"
  - line: 591
    type: narration
    text: "Below, a group of grove giants had positioned themselves near the old road, their smaller, denser forms silhouetted against the grey sky."
  - line: 592
    type: narration
    text: "They had been there for days, and unlike the swamp giants who patrolled restlessly, these stood still, almost meditative."
  - line: 593
    type: narration
    text: "Occasionally one would make a sound – a low rumble or a clicking that carried across the frozen marsh – and the others would shift their positions in response."
  - line: 595
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“Renn’s scouts say they’ve built something in the highlands,”"
  - line: 597
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn felt a chill that had nothing to do with the cold."
  - line: 598
    type: narration
    text: "The grove giants were not just intelligent; they were learning."
  - line: 599
    type: narration
    text: "Adapting."
  - line: 600
    type: narration
    text: "Using what they had observed."
  - line: 602
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“We need to make contact,”"
  - line: 604
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“Sera’s been practicing,”"
  - line: 606
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn nodded slowly."
  - line: 607
    type: narration
    text: "The Aeon Keepers had given them the tools; now they had to learn to use them."
  - line: 609
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“Tomorrow,”"
  - line: 611
    type: narration
    text: "Kael’s expression tightened, but he didn’t argue."
  - line: 613
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 615
    type: narration
    text: "X."
  - line: 616
    type: narration
    text: "The Boundary"
  - line: 618
    type: narration
    text: "They walked out at dawn, when the light was grey and the giants were most active."
  - line: 620
    type: narration
    text: "The boundary was marked by the ancient stone road that ringed the plaza – a line of moss‑covered blocks that the swamp giants never crossed."
  - line: 621
    type: narration
    text: "The grove giants had positioned themselves a short distance beyond it, their bodies still as the rocks they resembled."
  - line: 623
    type: narration
    text: "Sera walked at the front, her hands empty, her voice a low hum that seemed to vibrate in Teryn’s chest."
  - line: 624
    type: narration
    text: "The crystal shard she carried – a fragment from the needle’s outer wall – glowed with a soft, steady light."
  - line: 626
    type: narration
    text: "The grove giants watched them approach."
  - line: 627
    type: narration
    text: "There were several of them, ranging from perhaps eighteen to twenty‑five feet tall."
  - line: 628
    type: narration
    text: "Their hides were the color of cooled lava, shot through with veins of obsidian that caught the weak sunlight."
  - line: 629
    type: narration
    text: "Unlike the swamp giants, whose faces were almost featureless, these had defined features – ridges above the eyes, mouths that could shape sounds, and eyes that held something Teryn had not expected: awareness."
  - line: 631
    type: narration
    text: "Sera stopped at the boundary."
  - line: 632
    type: narration
    text: "Her humming rose, becoming a melody that wove through the morning air."
  - line: 633
    type: narration
    text: "The crystal shard pulsed in rhythm."
  - line: 635
    type: narration
    text: "One of the giants – the largest, with a pattern of white crystal tracing its jaw – took a step forward."
  - line: 636
    type: narration
    text: "Its head tilted, its eyes fixed on Sera."
  - line: 637
    type: narration
    text: "Then it opened its mouth and produced a sound."
  - line: 639
    type: narration
    text: "It was not a roar or a grunt."
  - line: 640
    type: narration
    text: "It was a note, clear and resonant, that matched the frequency of Sera’s melody."
  - line: 642
    type: narration
    text: "Sera’s humming faltered for a moment, then steadied."
  - line: 643
    type: narration
    text: "She changed the pitch, rising slowly through a scale."
  - line: 644
    type: narration
    text: "The giant followed, its voice rough but accurate, each note a fraction of a second behind hers."
  - line: 646
    type: narration
    text: "Behind Teryn, she heard Kael’s sharp intake of breath."
  - line: 648
    type: narration
    text: "The exchange continued for a short while – Sera offering sounds, the giant echoing them back."
  - line: 649
    type: narration
    text: "The other giants watched in silence, their heads moving slightly, as if listening to a conversation they could not yet understand."
  - line: 651
    type: narration
    text: "Then Sera did something new."
  - line: 652
    type: narration
    text: "She let her voice drop to a low, sustained note, and she pushed – not sound, but something deeper."
  - line: 653
    type: narration
    text: "Intention."
  - line: 654
    type: narration
    text: "The crystal shard blazed, and for a moment, the needle behind them pulsed in answer."
  - line: 656
    type: narration
    text: "The giant’s eyes widened."
  - line: 657
    type: narration
    text: "It took a step back, and Teryn’s hand went to the stone knife at her belt before she could stop herself."
  - line: 659
    type: narration
    text: "But the giant did not attack."
  - line: 660
    type: narration
    text: "It looked at Sera, then at the needle, then back at Sera."
  - line: 661
    type: narration
    text: "Its mouth opened again, and this time the sound it made was not an echo."
  - line: 662
    type: narration
    text: "It was a new note, one Sera had not offered – a deep, questioning tone that seemed to ask something."
  - line: 664
    type: narration
    text: "Sera answered."
  - line: 665
    type: narration
    text: "Her voice softened, the melody becoming something gentle, something that in the language of the settlement meant peace."
  - line: 667
    type: narration
    text: "The giant held the note for a long moment."
  - line: 668
    type: narration
    text: "Then it turned and walked back to its companions."
  - line: 669
    type: narration
    text: "The group of them stood together, and for a heartbeat, Teryn thought she saw them lean toward each other, as if sharing something without words."
  - line: 671
    type: narration
    text: "Then, as one, they turned and walked south, toward the highlands."
  - line: 673
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“They’re leaving,”"
  - line: 675
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“Not leaving,”"
  - line: 677
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn watched until the giants disappeared into the mist."
  - line: 678
    type: narration
    text: "Then she turned to Sera, whose face was pale with exhaustion but whose eyes were bright."
  - line: 680
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“What did you say to them?”"
  - line: 682
    type: narration
    text: "Sera shook her head slowly."
  - line: 683
    type: narration
    text: "“I don’t know."
  - line: 684
    type: narration
    text: "I just… sang."
  - line: 685
    type: narration
    text: "And they listened.”"
  - line: 687
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 689
    type: narration
    text: "XI."
  - line: 690
    type: narration
    text: "Echoes"
  - line: 692
    type: narration
    text: "The grove giants did not return to the boundary in the days that followed."
  - line: 694
    type: narration
    text: "The swamp giants remained, their patrols circling the plaza at a distance, but they seemed unsettled – more restless, more aggressive in their movements."
  - line: 695
    type: narration
    text: "Twice, scouts reported that they had gathered in large numbers near the eastern marsh, making sounds that carried across the water."
  - line: 697
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“They’re agitated,”"
  - line: 698
    type: narration
    text: "Renn reported. “Whatever happened at the boundary, they felt it. They don’t like it.”"
  - line: 700
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn stood with him on the wall, watching the distant shapes move through the morning mist."
  - line: 701
    type: narration
    text: "“The grove giants understood something."
  - line: 702
    type: narration
    text: "The swamp giants don’t."
  - line: 703
    type: narration
    text: "That makes them dangerous.”"
  - line: 705
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“Or desperate,”"
  - line: 707
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“Heard it how?”"
  - line: 709
    type: narration
    text: "Kael’s expression was troubled."
  - line: 710
    type: narration
    text: "“The crystal veins are more active."
  - line: 711
    type: narration
    text: "The light is brighter, the rhythm steadier."
  - line: 712
    type: narration
    text: "It’s like… like the needle is waking up."
  - line: 713
    type: narration
    text: "Slowly.”"
  - line: 715
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn looked at the spire behind her."
  - line: 716
    type: narration
    text: "Its core still leaked pale light, still pulsed with that labored rhythm, but there was something different about it now."
  - line: 717
    type: narration
    text: "A sense of presence that had not been there before."
  - line: 719
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“The chamber,”"
  - line: 721
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“The fissure is clear,”"
  - line: 723
    type: narration
    text: "She nodded."
  - line: 724
    type: narration
    text: "“Sera."
  - line: 725
    type: narration
    text: "Renn."
  - line: 726
    type: narration
    text: "You, me."
  - line: 727
    type: narration
    text: "The same group."
  - line: 728
    type: narration
    text: "We find out what’s behind that door.”"
  - line: 730
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 732
    type: narration
    text: "XII."
  - line: 733
    type: narration
    text: "The Door"
  - line: 735
    type: narration
    text: "The descent was easier this time."
  - line: 736
    type: narration
    text: "The passage was still narrow, still cold, but the bioluminescence of the crystal veins was brighter, casting enough light that they didn’t need their own."
  - line: 738
    type: narration
    text: "The chamber was transformed."
  - line: 740
    type: narration
    text: "The pool had receded further, exposing a ring of stone around the door."
  - line: 741
    type: narration
    text: "The door itself was no longer submerged – its upper half rose above the water, its surface rippling with light that seemed to pulse in rhythm with the needle."
  - line: 742
    type: narration
    text: "The patterns on its surface were clearer now: spirals and waves that moved like living things, geometries that suggested dimensions beyond the physical."
  - line: 744
    type: narration
    text: "Sera knelt at the pool’s edge."
  - line: 745
    type: narration
    text: "“It’s waiting,” she said again, but this time her voice carried certainty."
  - line: 746
    type: narration
    text: "“It knows we’re here.”"
  - line: 748
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“What is it?”"
  - line: 750
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“The heart,”"
  - line: 752
    type: narration
    text: "He didn’t say “someone.” Teryn noted the distinction."
  - line: 754
    type: narration
    text: "Sera began to sing."
  - line: 756
    type: narration
    text: "It was not the tentative humming of their early days, or the careful echoing of the boundary."
  - line: 757
    type: narration
    text: "This was a song she had been building for months – layers of melody that wove together the work‑songs of the settlement, the calls that had brought survivors home, the note she had exchanged with the grove giant."
  - line: 758
    type: narration
    text: "It was the voice of the settlement itself, given form."
  - line: 760
    type: narration
    text: "The door answered."
  - line: 762
    type: narration
    text: "Light bloomed from its surface, bright enough to make them shield their eyes."
  - line: 763
    type: narration
    text: "The water in the pool began to move, not rising but spinning, forming a slow vortex that pulled at the edges of the door."
  - line: 764
    type: narration
    text: "And beneath the light, beneath the water, something stirred."
  - line: 766
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn felt it brush against her consciousness – vast, fragmented, aware but not awake."
  - line: 767
    type: narration
    text: "It was like touching the mind of a dreamer, someone who could feel the presence of others but could not fully rouse themselves."
  - line: 768
    type: narration
    text: "There was pain there, and confusion, and something else: a desperate, patient hope."
  - line: 770
    type: narration
    text: "Sing, it seemed to say."
  - line: 771
    type: narration
    text: "Sing and I will hear."
  - line: 773
    type: narration
    text: "Sera’s voice cracked."
  - line: 774
    type: narration
    text: "She was crying, tears streaming down her face, but she did not stop."
  - line: 775
    type: narration
    text: "The song grew stronger, and the door’s light grew with it."
  - line: 776
    type: narration
    text: "For a moment – a single, crystalline moment – Teryn saw through the door."
  - line: 778
    type: narration
    text: "Beyond it was not a chamber."
  - line: 779
    type: narration
    text: "It was a space that stretched into infinity, filled with crystal formations that pulsed with light."
  - line: 780
    type: narration
    text: "And at its center, a figure: not Nephoretti, not giant, but something older, something that had been there when the needle was built."
  - line: 781
    type: narration
    text: "Its form was indistinct, shifting between shapes, but its eyes were fixed on them."
  - line: 783
    type: narration
    text: "Then the water surged."
  - line: 784
    type: narration
    text: "A wave rose from the pool, crashing against the door, and the vision vanished."
  - line: 785
    type: narration
    text: "The light dimmed."
  - line: 786
    type: narration
    text: "The presence withdrew."
  - line: 788
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“We need to go,”"
  - line: 790
    type: narration
    text: "They scrambled up the passage, the water chasing them, and by the time they reached the surface, the fissure was already flooding behind them."
  - line: 792
    type: narration
    text: "Sera lay on the stone floor of the needle’s base, gasping, her face streaked with tears and water."
  - line: 793
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn knelt beside her."
  - line: 795
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“What did you see?”"
  - line: 797
    type: narration
    text: "Sera’s eyes were distant."
  - line: 798
    type: narration
    text: "“It’s hurt,” she whispered."
  - line: 799
    type: narration
    text: "“It’s been hurt for so long."
  - line: 800
    type: narration
    text: "It’s been waiting for someone to sing it awake.”"
  - line: 802
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“The Keeper,”"
  - line: 804
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn looked at the crystal veins pulsing in the walls."
  - line: 805
    type: narration
    text: "The light was stronger now, steadier, as if the song had fed it."
  - line: 807
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“Then we keep singing,”"
  - line: 809
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 811
    type: narration
    text: "XIII."
  - line: 812
    type: narration
    text: "The Turning"
  - line: 814
    type: narration
    text: "Spring took hold in earnest after that."
  - line: 816
    type: narration
    text: "The last snow melted from the highlands, and the rivers that had been frozen for months began to run clear."
  - line: 817
    type: narration
    text: "The swamp giants gradually withdrew to their territories, their aggression replaced by wariness."
  - line: 818
    type: narration
    text: "And the grove giants – those who had exchanged notes with Sera – returned to the boundary."
  - line: 820
    type: narration
    text: "Not to threaten."
  - line: 821
    type: narration
    text: "To watch."
  - line: 822
    type: narration
    text: "To listen."
  - line: 824
    type: narration
    text: "Every morning, Sera went to the old road and sang."
  - line: 825
    type: narration
    text: "Her voice carried across the marsh, and sometimes the giants answered – not with words, but with notes that matched hers, that echoed her melodies back to her."
  - line: 826
    type: narration
    text: "It was not language, not yet."
  - line: 827
    type: narration
    text: "But it was communication."
  - line: 829
    type: narration
    text: "In the settlement, the survivors worked through the spring, expanding the walls, planting the first crops in the cleared fields beyond the plaza, building a meeting hall where the council could gather."
  - line: 830
    type: narration
    text: "Several hundred had become more as survivors found their way home."
  - line: 831
    type: narration
    text: "The scouts reported that the remaining survivors – perhaps another hundred scattered across the continent – were slowly converging on the needle."
  - line: 833
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn stood on the wall one evening, watching the sunset paint the western sky in shades of orange and purple."
  - line: 834
    type: narration
    text: "The needle pulsed behind her, its light stronger than it had been since they arrived."
  - line: 835
    type: narration
    text: "The song had fed it."
  - line: 836
    type: narration
    text: "The contact with the grove giants had fed it."
  - line: 837
    type: narration
    text: "And beneath it all, The Keeper stirred in its dreaming, waiting for the moment when it would be strong enough to wake."
  - line: 839
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“We’re going to need a name for this place,”"
  - line: 841
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn smiled."
  - line: 842
    type: narration
    text: "“The Keepers called it the Garden.”"
  - line: 844
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Seems like a lot of work for a garden.”"
  - line: 845
    type: narration
    text: "Kael smirked."
  - line: 847
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“The best gardens are.”"
  - line: 849
    type: narration
    text: "Kael thought."
  - line: 850
    type: narration
    text: "“Garden Grove… That’s what we call it.”"
  - line: 852
    type: narration
    text: "They stood in silence for a moment, watching the last light fade."
  - line: 853
    type: narration
    text: "In the distance, a grove giant stood at the boundary, its silhouette dark against the sky."
  - line: 854
    type: narration
    text: "It made a sound – a low, resonant hum – and Sera’s voice answered from somewhere below."
  - line: 856
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“It’s beginning,”"
  - line: 858
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn nodded."
  - line: 859
    type: narration
    text: "The Second Song had found its voice."
  - line: 860
    type: narration
    text: "And somewhere beneath them, deep in the wounded heart of the needle, The Keeper listened."
  - line: 862
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 864
    type: narration
    text: "XIV."
  - line: 865
    type: narration
    text: "The Dividing Line"
  - line: 867
    type: narration
    text: "By midsummer, the marsh had transformed."
  - line: 869
    type: narration
    text: "What had been a place of survival became something approaching abundance."
  - line: 870
    type: narration
    text: "The channels that had frozen and flooded now teemed with fish."
  - line: 871
    type: narration
    text: "The twisted trees that lined the waterways put forth fruit that none of them recognized but all learned to eat."
  - line: 872
    type: narration
    text: "And the fields they had planted – laboriously, using vrill to turn the ancient soil – were beginning to show green."
  - line: 874
    type: narration
    text: "The settlement had grown with the season."
  - line: 875
    type: narration
    text: "Garden Grove now numbered several hundred, as the last of the scattered survivors found their way home."
  - line: 876
    type: narration
    text: "The wall had been extended twice, and the outer structures they had discovered in the winter – the old workshops, the ring of fallen columns – had been cleared and rebuilt."
  - line: 877
    type: narration
    text: "What had been a refuge was becoming a town."
  - line: 879
    type: narration
    text: "But the peace of summer was an illusion."
  - line: 881
    type: narration
    text: "Kael felt it first, as he always did."
  - line: 882
    type: narration
    text: "The pulse had been steady for weeks – stronger than at any time since their landing."
  - line: 883
    type: narration
    text: "But now there was something else beneath it."
  - line: 884
    type: narration
    text: "A vibration, low and constant, that came not from the needle but from the south."
  - line: 886
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“The grove giants,”"
  - line: 887
    type: narration
    text: "he told Teryn one evening, standing on the wall that faced the highlands. “They’re moving. Not patrolling. Something else.”"
  - line: 889
    type: narration
    text: "She followed his gaze."
  - line: 890
    type: narration
    text: "In the distance, dust rose from the ancient road that led to the mountains."
  - line: 891
    type: narration
    text: "Not the dust of wind, but of feet."
  - line: 892
    type: narration
    text: "Many feet."
  - line: 894
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“How many?”"
  - line: 896
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“Hard to say. Dozens. Maybe more.”"
  - line: 898
    type: narration
    text: "They watched in silence as the dust cloud grew, and with it, the low vibration that Kael had felt through the stone."
  - line: 900
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 902
    type: narration
    text: "XV."
  - line: 903
    type: narration
    text: "The Gathering of Giants"
  - line: 905
    type: narration
    text: "The grove giants came not to the boundary, but to the highlands themselves."
  - line: 907
    type: narration
    text: "Renn’s scouts returned with reports that turned the settlement’s attention from growth to war."
  - line: 908
    type: narration
    text: "The giants had gathered in the stone circle they had built over the winter – the one that mimicked the outer complex around the needle."
  - line: 909
    type: narration
    text: "But now there were more of them, and they had brought weapons."
  - line: 911
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“Not against us,”"
  - line: 913
    type: narration
    text: "He described what the scouts had seen: two factions among the grove giants, their hides marked with different patterns of crystal, their leaders standing at opposite ends of the circle."
  - line: 914
    type: narration
    text: "They had been arguing – if the sounds they made could be called arguing – for days."
  - line: 915
    type: narration
    text: "And now they were preparing for something worse."
  - line: 917
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“The swamp giants are watching,”"
  - line: 918
    type: narration
    text: "Renn continued. “They’ve pulled back from our boundary. They’re waiting to see which side wins.”"
  - line: 920
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn called the council that night."
  - line: 921
    type: narration
    text: "Sera came with her voice hoarse from singing, Kael with his hand pressed to the needle’s wall, Vairis with her ledgers of food and supplies, Renn with his maps."
  - line: 923
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“They’re going to fight,”"
  - line: 925
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Vairis
    text: "“Can we stop them?”"
  - line: 927
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Kael
    text: "“We barely understand them,”"
  - line: 929
    type: narration
    text: "Sera was quiet."
  - line: 930
    type: narration
    text: "She had been quiet since the council began, her eyes distant, her fingers tracing patterns on the table."
  - line: 932
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“Sera,”"
  - line: 934
    type: narration
    text: "She looked up slowly."
  - line: 935
    type: narration
    text: "“The grove giants are fighting because the pulse is changing."
  - line: 936
    type: narration
    text: "The needle is waking up, and they feel it."
  - line: 937
    type: narration
    text: "Some of them want to protect it."
  - line: 938
    type: narration
    text: "Some of them want to use it."
  - line: 939
    type: narration
    text: "The swamp giants… they don’t understand."
  - line: 940
    type: narration
    text: "They only know that something is different, and they’re afraid.”"
  - line: 942
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“Can we talk to them?”"
  - line: 944
    type: narration
    text: "Sera shook her head."
  - line: 945
    type: narration
    text: "“They’re not ready."
  - line: 946
    type: narration
    text: "They need something first."
  - line: 947
    type: narration
    text: "A sign."
  - line: 948
    type: narration
    text: "A reason to trust us.”"
  - line: 950
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“What kind of sign?”"
  - line: 952
    type: narration
    text: "Sera looked at Kael, then at the wall where the needle’s pulse flickered."
  - line: 953
    type: narration
    text: "“The Keeper."
  - line: 954
    type: narration
    text: "If The Keeper wakes – even for a moment – they’ll see."
  - line: 955
    type: narration
    text: "They’ll understand.”"
  - line: 957
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn felt the weight of what Sera was asking."
  - line: 958
    type: narration
    text: "The chamber beneath the needle, the door, the presence that had stirred when Sera sang."
  - line: 959
    type: narration
    text: "They had been planning to go back, to try again, but the water had risen with the spring melt."
  - line: 960
    type: narration
    text: "It would be weeks before the pool receded enough to reach the door."
  - line: 962
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“We don’t have weeks,”"
  - line: 964
    type: dialogue
    speaker: unknown
    text: "“No,”"
  - line: 965
    type: narration
    text: "Sera agreed. “But we don’t need the door. The Keeper can hear us through the pulse. If we sing together – all of us – it will hear. It might answer.”"
  - line: 967
    type: narration
    text: "The council fell silent."
  - line: 968
    type: narration
    text: "They had never attempted anything like this."
  - line: 969
    type: narration
    text: "Sera’s voice had carried to the survivors, had reached the grove giants at the boundary."
  - line: 970
    type: narration
    text: "But to wake The Keeper?"
  - line: 971
    type: narration
    text: "To call across the dimensions that separated it from them?"
  - line: 973
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Teryn
    text: "“We do it tomorrow,”"
  - line: 975
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 977
    type: narration
    text: "XVI."
  - line: 978
    type: narration
    text: "The Song of the Grove"
  - line: 980
    type: narration
    text: "The settlement gathered at the base of the needle as the sun rose."
  - line: 982
    type: narration
    text: "Hundreds of Nephoretti, their bioluminescence fading in the growing light, their voices uncertain."
  - line: 983
    type: narration
    text: "Sera stood at the front, her hand on the largest crystal vein, her eyes closed."
  - line: 984
    type: narration
    text: "Beside her, Kael pressed his palm to the stone, feeling the pulse."
  - line: 986
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Sera
    text: "“Sing what you know,”"
  - line: 988
    type: narration
    text: "She began, her voice rising in the morning air."
  - line: 989
    type: narration
    text: "It was not the careful humming of the boundary, or the desperate song of winter."
  - line: 990
    type: narration
    text: "It was something older, something that seemed to come from the stone itself."
  - line: 992
    type: narration
    text: "One by one, the others joined."
  - line: 993
    type: narration
    text: "Kael’s voice, rough from disuse, found a harmony with Vairis’s steady tone."
  - line: 994
    type: narration
    text: "Renn’s scouts sang of the highlands, of the caves where they had hidden, of the journeys that had brought them home."
  - line: 995
    type: narration
    text: "Darian’s eastern group sang of the hills, of the frozen roots that had kept them alive, of the pulse that had called them through the snow."
  - line: 997
    type: narration
    text: "The needle answered."
  - line: 999
    type: narration
    text: "Light bloomed in the crystal veins, brighter than any of them had seen since the landing."
  - line: 1000
    type: narration
    text: "The pulse quickened, steadied, and for a moment – a single, crystalline moment – the spire itself seemed to hum."
  - line: 1002
    type: narration
    text: "Then the ground shook."
  - line: 1004
    type: narration
    text: "It was not the giants, though Teryn’s hand went to her knife."
  - line: 1005
    type: narration
    text: "It was deeper, older, a vibration that came from the stone itself."
  - line: 1006
    type: narration
    text: "The fissure that led to the chamber – the one that had flooded and receded and flooded again – split wider, and water began to pour from it."
  - line: 1007
    type: narration
    text: "Not the stagnant water of the pool, but something clear, something that shone with the same light as the crystal veins."
  - line: 1009
    type: narration
    text: "And from the fissure, a sound."
  - line: 1011
    type: narration
    text: "It was not a voice, not exactly."
  - line: 1012
    type: narration
    text: "It was a note, pure and resonant, that matched the frequency of Sera’s song."
  - line: 1013
    type: narration
    text: "It held for a long moment, and in that moment, Teryn felt something brush against her consciousness: a presence, vast and patient, aware at last."
  - line: 1015
    type: narration
    text: "Then the note faded."
  - line: 1016
    type: narration
    text: "The water stopped flowing."
  - line: 1017
    type: narration
    text: "The pulse returned to its steady rhythm."
  - line: 1019
    type: narration
    text: "But something had changed."
  - line: 1021
    type: scene_header
    text: "---"
  - line: 1023
    type: narration
    text: "XVII."
  - line: 1024
    type: narration
    text: "The First Blood"
  - line: 1026
    type: narration
    text: "The grove giants came to the boundary that afternoon."
  - line: 1028
    type: narration
    text: "Not the few who had exchanged notes with Sera, but a larger group – several dozen, their hides marked with the crystal patterns that Renn’s scouts had described."
  - line: 1029
    type: narration
    text: "They moved with purpose, their weapons – stone axes, obsidian‑tipped spears – held not toward the settlement, but toward the south."
  - line: 1031
    type: narration
    text: "Behind them, the highlands were burning."
  - line: 1033
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn saw it from the wall: smoke rising from the stone circle where the grove giants had gathered, and beyond it, movement."
  - line: 1034
    type: narration
    text: "The swamp giants had chosen a side."
  - line: 1036
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Renn
    text: "“The ones who want to protect the needle,”"
  - line: 1038
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Vairis
    text: "“What do they want?”"
  - line: 1040
    type: narration
    text: "Kael pressed his hand to the wall."
  - line: 1041
    type: narration
    text: "“Shelter."
  - line: 1042
    type: narration
    text: "The pulse keeps the swamp giants away."
  - line: 1043
    type: narration
    text: "They know that.”"
  - line: 1045
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn looked at the grove giants."
  - line: 1046
    type: narration
    text: "They were battered, some of them bleeding from wounds that leaked light instead of blood."
  - line: 1047
    type: narration
    text: "Their leader – the one with the white crystal tracing its jaw – stood at the front, its eyes fixed on the needle."
  - line: 1048
    type: narration
    text: "It opened its mouth and made a sound: the note Sera had sung at dawn, the one The Keeper had answered."
  - line: 1050
    type: dialogue
    speaker: Sera
    text: "“They’re asking for help,”"
  - line: 1052
    type: narration
    text: "Teryn looked at the wall, at the hundreds of survivors who had just sung The Keeper awake."
  - line: 1053
    type: narration
    text: "She looked at the grove giants, wounded and desperate, and at the smoke rising from their home."
  - line: 1055
    type: dialogue
    speaker: she
    text: "“Open the gate,”"
  - line: 1057
    type: narration
    text: "end of chapter 104-the rising tide"

